 CellID->683,ExpressionUUID->"4b5955b4-6a6d-421a-8a03-060063c2a7b7"],

Cell["\<\
GetData[name] uncompresses the stored entry, validates it as a solution and \
returns it. Nothing is defined in xAct until Load is called on the result.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->684,ExpressionUUID->"39b0e8d6-8bfe-417a-8814-6bba1c0c5b3c"],

Cell["\<\
A bare name is looked up under the user's own alias, silently and only there. \
Another user's entry is read explicitly, as GetData[\"alias/name\"] or with \
the option Alias -> \"alias\"; entry names never contain a slash, so the form \
is unambiguous.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->685,ExpressionUUID->"5813b4e8-88fd-4c43-bb48-43857524f1b4"],

Cell["\<\
GetData[] takes the alias and the name from the directory containing the \
current notebook, which is where SaveData put it. This is the usual way a \
notebook reloads its own entry -- and it works for anyone running the \
notebook, whoever owns the entry.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->686,ExpressionUUID->"8cefab7b-83a1-41b9-ae8e-96ed20e9e43f"],

Cell["\<\
Only one solution can be loaded at a time: two entries built on the same \
theory share the symbols of that theory, and loading both collides. The \
established practice is to load one and read the other passively, as data, \
through full[object, key, Expression] and Gen[full[object, key]].\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->687,ExpressionUUID->"03e6c7b7-2b12-43e7-9ab6-9039d7232c10"],

Cell["\<\
A passively held solution is an ordinary variable, not part of the loaded \
state, so it must be fetched again after every reload.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->688,ExpressionUUID->"8ea2fce7-db81-4534-b8ed-2c7e1cae0b55"],

Cell["\<\
GetData issues GetData::missingname if the entry is not found under the \
current $Alias.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->689,ExpressionUUID->"35fe84b7-badb-4beb-b7a2-ea5e639b1a73"]
}, Open  ]],

